  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SINTEF C &amp; D Waste Treatment-Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The phase-I of the support was to generate interest and build capacity of the government agencies on sustainably managing construction and demolition waste in India. The objective of Phase II is to demonstrate sound and safe treatment, recycling and utilisation of Construction and Demolition waste (C&amp;D) waste.The state of Goa would be the focal point in the project so so as to demonstrate a functional treatment facility. Goa&apos;s booming tourism industry demanded newer buildings which has resulted in C&amp;D waste and lack of treatment facility. The Goa Waste Management Corporation (GWDC) realized the need for the treatment of C&amp;D waste and has engaged with SINTEF and has signed a MoU for technical support. The project is also expected to support in creating a national guideline for quality control for C&amp;D facilities. 
The target groups are the GWDC, the Central Public Works Department, Mionistry of Environment Forests &amp; Climate Change and the national construction industry.</narrative>
  </description>
